 plan review — before this leaf is accepted, since the leaf's advisory scope contradicts the parent's 'parallel Verified lane' wording.","cohort":["G7"],"criteria":["G7"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.18,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent 78f2 AC: '[RP14/T07] Pinned deployed Semgrep and Gitleaks integrations run in a portable direct-binary parallel Verified lane.'","Leaf AC: 'Gerrit scanner wiring is non-voting/non-blocking: separate workflow, outside gerrit-verify.yaml, outside vote.needs, outside vote normalization, and outside required workflow-conclusion aggregation.'","Leaf Context: 'scanner integration must not enter the required Verified hot path. ADR 0114 requires this lane to run advisory first'","Epic updated_at 1788582803684178001 predates the leaf's advisory-rescope comment (1788584410167881001), so the parent AC text was never revised; the epic's plan-review manifest still pins 'child aa9e-3d35-fd3e-41ee dc9edfb0c92b4637'.","CONFLICT RULE: parent is authoritative; leaf now delivers work (advisory, outside Verified) the parent AC does not contain and contradicts the parent clause 'Verified lane'."],"finding":"The leaf redefines/contradicts parent epic AC RP14/T07, which mandates the scanner integrations 'run in a portable direct-binary parallel Verified lane', by delivering an intentionally ADVISORY, non-voting lane explicitly OUTSIDE the required Verified aggregate (outside gerrit-verify.yaml, vote.needs, vote normalization, and the workflow-conclusion snapshot). The parent AC still reads 'Verified lane' verbatim and was not updated to reflect the ADR-0114 advisory-first rescope; the epic's plan-review attestation still pins the older child material.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f30d1efd100c27b99","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Leaf 'Advisory wiring contract' + ACs ('Gerrit scanner wiring is non-voting/non-blocking ... outside required workflow-conclusion aggregation') vs parent epic 78f2 AC '[RP14/T07] ... 