"- [ ] State the disposition for a transient installer-download failure (retryable/transient — safe to re-run) versus a permanent integrity/withdrawn-asset failure (fatal — requires manifest update), so advisory-lane operators can distinguish a re-run from a real regression.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T5b","project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4187,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'installer uses pip install --require-hashes' and 'exact Gitleaks URLs and SHA-256 values' — a network fetch with integrity check","docs AC covers only 'withdrawn-asset recovery procedure' (permanent), not transient fetch failure","The lane is advisory/non-blocking, which caps blast radius — a flaky download fails only the advisory job, not the required Verified vote"],"finding":"The installer performs external downloads of Gitleaks/Semgrep artifacts (pip --require-hashes, release URLs by digest). The plan documents a permanent 'withdrawn-asset recovery procedure' but does not state the disposition for a TRANSIENT download failure (network flake / rate-limited mirror) versus a permanent integrity failure — no retry/timeout posture is named for the advisory lane's external fetches.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcfcc0a4063fb9f2a","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope: 'scanner installer'; AC 'Installer rejects ... wrong Gitleaks version/digest, and invalid Semgrep hashes'; docs 'withdrawn-asset recovery procedure'","norm_id":"n3c5522140fc104d4","priority":0.4813,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"