 90c7 comment #10): 'a relative symlink target is resolved relative to the symlink's OWN DIRECTORY, so the link resolves to .tools/review-scanners/bin/.tools/review-scanners/semgrep-venv/bin/semgrep — nonexistent... The symlink is created successfully and DANGLES'; the diagnosis names the minimal fix ('link.symlink_to(semgrep.resolve())') and the class fix ('resolve the prefix once at the boundary').","Plan scope: 'Recreate/adapt the reverted scanner integration' — the reverted install_review_scanners.py contained this exact latent bug in every prefix-override call site.","AC7 constrains the outcome (bin/semgrep executable) but the plan states no mechanism, so an implementer could reproduce the buggy _link_semgrep and treat the RED test as sufficient rather than fixing the resolution."],"finding":"The plan requires the relative-prefix bin/semgrep behavior to hold (AC7 + scope bullet) but never names the actual fix for the incident's root-cause Fault 3 — the dangling RELATIVE symlink _link_semgrep created under a relative --prefix — so 'recreate/adapt the reverted scanner integration' risks re-landing the buggy installer verbatim and relying only on the new test to catch it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa0b5febaaaa299d5","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope bullet 'the relative-prefix Semgrep-link behavior...' and Acceptance Criteria line 7","norm_id":"nf5888acd9528c641","priority":0.134,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer recreates install_review_scanners.py faithfully from the reverted change, reintroducing the relative-symlink defect; the new test goes RED and the fix is then improvised without the boundary-resolve guidance, leaving other prefix-override call sites (check path, gitleaks work dir) latently broken."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add to scope/AC: the installer must resolve the selected prefix to an absolute path once at the boundary (e.g. _selected_prefix(...).resolve()) — or equivalen